  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "Writable.variable accepts any present slot; field resolves a parent uniquely and finds its field slot. Replaceable is True for none and StructReference for some. Write performs list-local replacement without reallocating objects or changing other fields/variables or nextId. It is a low-level relation used behind Writable/Replaceable guards by RawStep, not independently a well-typed transition. Rooted-foundation review: the structural invariants now require explicit rootedness (including pending values) plus unique/compatible ownership. Allocation bounds remain solely for freshness; no safety proof assumes edge-age order or global DAG structure. Changed proof selections retain their public statement unless this unit explicitly defines the revised invariant or example. Given/Shared root transport and path reasoning were reviewed by their implementing agents, with fresh review of root-owned unpacking, GC, frame rerooting, class retention and the refill example. Earlier syntax and runtime rules are unchanged. The widened invariant domain is covered by recompilation of all earlier safety proofs and concrete shared-cycle/nonmonotonic-ID regressions, not by a claim that constructors can generate cycles.",
  "limitations": [
    "Author integration review with agent review of Given/Shared foundations and fresh review of root-owned integration. Lean checks proof correctness separately.",
    "Assignment general safety remains deferred. Cyclic heap examples test invariant and operation scope, not source-program construction from the current empty initial state."
  ],
